WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.680
- In this video, I'd like
to give you a few tips

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:05.410
on how to behave on conference calls,

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.140
so that it is both effective

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.490
and also respectful to the
other members on the call.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.280
I trust this is going to
be especially relevant

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.650
in these times where
we know there are just

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.150
so much more conference
calls going on than usually.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.510
Hi guys, my name is Heinrich,

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.860
and welcome to another Coffee
Break with Firm Learning.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.550
Today I'm talking about conference calls.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.060
And as probably you know,

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.370
in consulting, conference
calls are so common,

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:33.350
you probably on a usual day

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:37.170
have more than five
conference calls going on.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.800
Since about half a year ago,

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.420
I make the move from
consulting moving into industry

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.570
and now I'm working for
a large German retailer.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.820
So I joined at the end of 2019

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:51.710
and at that time our
company was quite unusual

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:52.700
to conference calls.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.400
It was very much a more
classically consultive culture

00:00:56.396 --> 00:01:00.050
of people rather prefering to
either just call somebody up

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:03.230
or just meet in person in
order to discuss things.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:07.010
Where, for obvious reasons, this changed

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.600
due to the global
pandemic that is going on

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.330
and also hit Germany in a substantial way.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.590
Since several weeks now a large proportion

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.360
of our leadership team is in home office

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.860
and I work from home office as well.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.570
You're currently seeing me filming this

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.630
sitting in my home office in Munich.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.870
And this brought quite a
significant change in culture

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:31.630
in our organization, as now we
have daily conference calls.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:32.960
Every morning for instance,

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.220
there's a conference call check in

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.660
with the senior leadership
team of our company.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.940
And both in this retail company
I'm currently working with,

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.720
but also in consulting, I've been working

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.370
with several clients, I've
observed a whole number of habits

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:48.350
that people have on conference calls

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.380
which are just either disturbing

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.570
for the majority of the people,
or just plain ineffective

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:56.030
for the objective of the conference call.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:58.760
Namely having a good and
to the point discussion

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.320
of the topics at hand that
just need to be solved

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.980
by the team that is now
just talking together.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.542
So in this video I like
to give you five tips

00:02:06.542 --> 00:02:08.060
on what you can do

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:11.510
in order to make your
conference calls more effective

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.460
and less of an annoyance
to all the people on there.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:15.810
And if you find this useful

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.560
feel free to forward this video

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.500
to some of your co-workers as well

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.380
so that your conference call experience

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.410
hopefully improves for
your whole organization.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.270
So first thing,

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:28.360
and this might seem to be one
of the more obvious things.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.220
Go on mute.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.870
It is incredible to me that most people

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:36.530
who are dialed in on a
conference call are not on mute

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.430
and just have the microphone
on the whole time,

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.200
even though they are not talking.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.820
And this is irritating and disturbing

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.020
for some obvious reasons.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.210
Even though it might
be quiet where you sit

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.780
at the moment right now,
it can always happen

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:54.630
that an ambulance passes by your street

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.860
or there's some other sudden noises

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:00.770
that suddenly come up that
then disturb the whole call.

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:04.410
And even if there not some
hidden sudden loud noises,

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.563
just you sitting in
front of your computer,

00:03:06.563 --> 00:03:11.180
pressing buttons on your
keyboard, maybe eating something,

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:14.530
maybe your neighbor's saying
something in a loud way,

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.320
all of these are things
which are disturbing,

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:20.580
which create a constant
level of background noise,

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.320
which is just not helpful

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.846
when you want to have a good discussion

00:03:23.846 --> 00:03:25.860
in your conference call.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:30.860
So my first advice is whenever
you do not talk, go on mute.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.780
This is the absolute
minimum that you need to do

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.970
in order to be respectful
to your other co-workers.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.340
Go on mute and unmute yourself

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.990
just whenever you really
need to say something.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.130
And if you don't need to
say something, go on mute

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:48.780
to not let other people be disturbed

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:52.010
by the background noises
that you will have

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:54.280
while being on the microphone.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.430
Now the second tip.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:58.380
And this is something that
I think we all know as well.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.350
And to what extent this issue exists

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:02.780
also depends on the conference call system

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:03.970
that you are using.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.670
But very frequently you
hear in the background

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:10.100
these automated voices of
the conference call system

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.887
saying something like,
"Peter joined the call."

00:04:13.887 --> 00:04:15.507
"Peter dropped the call."

00:04:15.507 --> 00:04:16.922
"Peter joined the call."

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.270
"Peter dropped the call."

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.670
So whenever somebody
joins or drops the call,

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.900
in many conference call systems,

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.040
there's an automated voice saying that

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:28.630
to all the people in the call.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.140
And of course if you've been there,

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:31.770
if you've seen these kind of things,

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.630
this is extremely disturbing

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:37.020
because if somebody
joins or drops the call,

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:41.090
basically the conversation
is interrupted by that voice.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.900
So how can you diminish this disturbance

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.340
as much as possible?

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.700
Well, and again, this
very much also depends

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.290
on the conference call
system that you're using,

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.920
how exactly that works.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.860
But frequently whenever you
dial into a conference call,

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.870
the system often asks you for your name.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:00.767
So let's say something like,

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.380
"Please tell us your
name after the beep sound

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.490
and then press the hash button."

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.660
Right, so it asks you to say your name

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.120
and then press the button,
usually the hash key

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.330
so that the system knows

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.490
that now the recording
can stop of your name.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:15.830
So what you need to do,
with a little trick here

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:18.880
is that when you're being
asked to tell your name,

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.180
just don't tell your name.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:24.130
Just don't say anything and
directly press the hash key.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.660
So it asks you, then you directly press it

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.250
without any second left

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.400
so that it cannot really record anything

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.490
and then when you join or
when you drop the call,

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:36.220
there will just be no sound of the system

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:38.050
saying your name to everybody

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:40.820
because this recording of
your name just doesn't exist.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.230
So whenever the system
asks you for your name,

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.060
press the hash key, don't say your name,

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.440
and you will be fine.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.860
Of course if there's a
strict rule in your company

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:52.850
that you need to say your
name, well then do that,

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.290
don't get in trouble for that.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.303
But most companies, there
isn't anything like that,

00:05:56.303 --> 00:05:58.950
and I can tell you if you do this

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:01.130
and if you tell your
co-workers to do this,

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:04.470
your conference calls
will go much more smoothly

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:08.890
because this kind of disturbance
just isn't there anymore.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.570
So guys my third tip is about what to do

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.330
when you actually join
the conference call late.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.560
And of course this can happen
for all kinds of reasons,

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.220
but what many people do,

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:22.610
which I find quite
disrespectful and disturbing,

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:27.230
is the person's late, the
discussion is already ongoing,

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:29.600
and then the person joins the call

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:31.197
and then just says something like,

00:06:31.197 --> 00:06:35.777
"Hi guys, Heinrich here,
I'm late, sorry for that.

00:06:35.777 --> 00:06:38.967
"I was just stuck in
traffic, but now I'm here.

00:06:38.967 --> 00:06:39.990
"Sorry for that. "

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:43.180
Right, and by doing that he disrupts,

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:45.830
he interrupts the whole conversation

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.500
and just stops the person
who was currently doing.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.020
And especially in large conference calls,

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.730
where there are many
people online in the call

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:55.470
and many people coming late,

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:59.100
if all these people then
apologized for being late

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.970
and then in the worst case
even also give a reason

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:05.730
why they were late, this
is just such a disturbance.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:09.080
So from my experience, the
best practice really is,

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.250
if you are joining the conference call

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:15.340
and you are late, just say nothing.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:18.460
Don't introduce yourself
that you are there now.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:22.770
Don't apologize why you
are late, just say nothing.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:25.340
And this is especially
true if you can hear

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.150
that the call already started

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.920
and there's already a
conversation going on.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.170
And of course, that might be
different if you are the CEO

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:35.620
of the company or if you are the person

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.720
who is actually supposed to
lead the whole conference call.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:41.293
You're just the most
important person in the call,

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:43.480
then maybe it's okay and
then maybe makes sense

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.670
that you let all the others
know that you are there.

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:48.710
But if you are just one
of many participants,

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.310
most likely be others will not really care

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:52.520
if you're there or not.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.930
Or at least they won't
care as much for you

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.110
to interrupt the whole discussion

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:58.410
just for letting them know.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.590
So just be quiet and just
use the next opportunity

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:02.630
where you see a moment

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:05.050
when you can just add something meaningful

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.407
to the discussion, where you can say that

00:08:07.407 --> 00:08:09.263
and then also by doing that
letting the others know

00:08:09.263 --> 00:08:11.400
that now you joined the call as well.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:15.960
The fourth tip on conference
calls is to be concise.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.910
So for all these reasons and many others,

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:23.300
conference calls can be
quite tiresome and annoying.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:26.220
Everybody should contribute
for making these calls

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.600
as short and as efficient as possible.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:32.880
And we all know these
people who just in meetings

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.860
and conversations need
to have their stage time.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:38.160
These people that feel
like that they always need

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.780
to say something that even though

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:42.070
that has been already said many times,

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:44.260
they need to repeat it again.

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:48.760
People that state the obvious
just to say something.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.330
This is annoying and
this is not only annoying

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.810
in conference calls, but of course also

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.660
in regular meetings as well.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:58.690
But this is especially
annoying in conference calls

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:01.120
because conference calls
in itself often are a bit

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:04.860
of an annoying situation and
this only makes it worse.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:07.020
So make sure that when you say something

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:09.430
it really adds value to the conversation,

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:11.170
you're not just repeating things

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:12.518
that others have already said.

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:15.020
You're not stating the obvious.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.720
So things that are completely obvious

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.010
but you just say them just

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.430
because you feel like you
need to say something.

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:22.210
Do not do these things.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:25.560
Be concise for the sake
of everybody involved.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:29.040
And now my fifth tip
is, if any how possible,

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.270
only join the call if you have a more

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.820
or less stable connection.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:36.790
I mean also we've all
been in these situations

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.850
where people join from an airport,

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:41.190
maybe already sitting in an airplane,

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:45.000
or they join from the car,
or they join from the train,

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.000
and then they constantly
lose the connection,

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:51.370
drop off the call, then drop in again.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.480
And this is just a disturbance

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.920
because even if you do not say
your name at the beginning,

00:09:56.920 --> 00:10:00.340
so it does not always say
"Peter joined or left the call."

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.590
Often there's at least the beeping sound

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:04.210
which is a disturbance.

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.130
So if you already know

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:08.540
that you will not have a stable connection

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.390
for your telephone conference

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:12.270
and if there's any way for you

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:16.250
that may be your attendance
isn't absolutely crucial,

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:17.980
or maybe there's a way to
postpone it to a moment

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:20.850
where you actually have
a more stable connection.

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.430
Do not join if your connection is unstable

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.260
because again, it is a big disturbance

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.390
to all the other people on the call.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.860
It is annoying and it's a waste of time,

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:32.730
so be respectful to the
time of your co-workers.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.720
So, these were my five tips.

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:37.030
And of course I'm interested now to hear

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:40.700
how has your work environment
changing in these dire times,

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.230
in this global pandemic?

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:44.200
Is it true for you as well

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.610
that you are now having
many more conference calls?

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:50.220
Let me know what your experience
is below in the comments.

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:53.720
I'd love to hear from you and
if you have any other tips

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:56.150
that you'd like to
share with our community

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:58.570
here on Firm Learning, let us know.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:01.350
I'm sure that others
would appreciate as well

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.700
what are your do's and
don'ts for having good

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:07.660
and effective telephone conferences.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:10.750
And of course, if you took
